  "query_preview": "..\n(Wednesday through next Monday)\nIssued at 138 PM CDT Mon Sep 28 2026\n\nThe advertised pattern change is on track for mid to late week with \nincreased showers and thunderstorm chances beginning Wednesday and \ncontinuing through late week and beyond. An upper low will be \nlocated over the Four Corners region Wednesday, eventually moving \neast across the Central and Southern Plains late week bringing a \nPacific cold front across our area. Abundant moisture will be \navailable ahead of this system with some guidance showing PWATs \naround 200 percent above normal. As to be expected with a strong \nupper low, models still vary to a certain degree on its progression \nand speed with the ECMWF continuing its slower trend compared to the \nGFS. We're starting to get a glimpse into hi-res guidance as this \nevent comes closer giving higher confidence to heavy rain in our \narea beginning more late Wednesday night in the west and Thursday in \nthe east. \n\nAhead of an expected line of storms during this timeframe, isolated \nto scattered thunderstorm activity will be possible across much of \nthe area as moderate onshore flow and hot and humid conditions \npersist Wednesday. Heat index values exceed 100 degrees for a \nmajority of the area in the afternoon capped under mostly cloudy \nskies with a breezy southeasterly wind. Any thunderstorm activity \nwill have a heavy rain threat given the environment and cannot rule \nout some gusty wind or hail as well.\n\nReturning to the Pacific front and the main focus of the extended \nforecast, expect this feature to slowly move across our area late \nWednesday night through Friday. Thunderstorms are likely to develop \nalong the southwest to northeast orientation of the front and could \nproduce heavy rainfall leading to flash flooding. There remains \nuncertainty in how quickly this front moves, how far it progresses, \nand where the heaviest rain will fall over the area. An upper low \nremains to the west Friday into Saturday with continued high \nmoisture residing over the area. This keeps medium to high rain \nchances over the area Friday into the weekend with high uncertainty \non details this far out. Temperatures Friday into the weekend should \nfall into the mid 70s and 80s given the rain chances and expected \ncloud cover. While details remain blurred for our late week system, \ncontinue to monitor the forecast and be prepared for potential heavy \nrainfall.",
